====================================================================================
PART 1: the c_t(t,r)=0 (t>r) plateau-killing identity (EXACT, the slack lever)
====================================================================================
c_t(t,r) = sum_i (-1)^i C(t,i)((7-i)/7)^r  = Pr[r iid far cover all t missing sectors]
  Proven: c_t(t,r)=0 for t>r (r runners hit <= r sectors); c_t(0,r)=1; increasing in r.
  exact check c_t(t,r)=0 for all t>r, r=0..6: PASS (0 violations)

  Consequence: p0_decorr(B,r) = sum_{t=0}^{r} prof_t(B) c_t(t,r).
  Mass of prof(B) at t>r is KILLED. A SPREAD/SMALL base puts mass at HIGH t,
  so when r is moderate the decorrelated cover is far below the dense (consec) plateau.

